# {{context_name}}

This repository holds {{context_name}}, a Context Fabric organization context. Governed facts live in its documents and generated views. Never hand-edit a generated view.

## Using the context

Start at the view's own instruction, [{{view_agents_path}}]({{view_agents_path}}). Follow its task-time safeguards and use only the named view, your Individual document and any retention sidecar for framework context. Reading needs no setup.

## Creating, maintaining or setting up the context

1. Find your Individual document the way the view's instruction describes, and select the binding for this workspace. Take its `framework_root`.
2. Read a skill by name under that root: `skill:<name>` is the file `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Begin with `skill:start-here`, then use `skill:develop-org`, `skill:setup-individual` or `skill:validate-and-generate` for the task.
3. With no binding, extract a no-clone bundle into this workspace (its skills use the same layout), or obtain {{framework_url}} as a checkout outside this repository at the ref recorded in [docs/maintenance.md](docs/maintenance.md), then follow `skill:setup-individual`.

A repository URL alone does not install skills. Without local execution a draft is not validated and no view is generated; say so.

Machine paths and secret references belong only in your Individual document, never in this repository.
